{{!-- Move-roll / description chat card. Data object: { name, icon?, dice?, outcome?, description?,
      resultText?, results?, applied?, xpLine? }.
      dice = { rolls:[{result,classes}], modeLabel, mod, formula, total, rollMode }. `rolls` is
      Foundry's OWN dice data, drawn with Foundry's own markup and die faces — the classes carry the
      die's size, its min/max face and whether a keep-modifier discarded it, none of which the card
      used to say. `mod` is what
      the dice did not account for — the rating a move added, or the rating a season step's formula
      resolved to — without which a card can show a 1 beside a total of 0 and explain neither.
      `formula` is the roll as the sheet NAMED it ("1d4 + Population"), for a card titled by what the
      roll did rather than by what it rolled; it takes the outcome's place in the readout, so a roll
      with no tier has something to say there instead of a gap. outcome = RollOutcome
      ({key, label}) — the tier the roll landed in, shown as a badge beside the total rather than
      appended to the name, so the headline stays the move's own name and wraps once at most.
      description/resultText are RichText (enriched by renderRollCard). results = [{ key, label,
      text }] — ALL tiers, for description-only cards (a roll card carries the single rolled tier
      as resultText instead).

      Order is result-then-description: on a roll card the tier text is the answer, and the move's
      full text is reference you have usually just read on the sheet. A description-only card has
      no resultText, so it still reads name → description → every tier. --}}
{{!-- Same icon the sheets show, from the same move data. --}}
<h3 class="stonetop-roll-title">{{name}}</h3>
{{#if dice}}
<div class="stonetop-roll-line{{#if outcome}} stonetop-roll-line--{{outcome.key}}{{else}} stonetop-roll-line--plain{{/if}}">
	<span class="stonetop-roll-total">{{dice.total}}</span>
	<div class="stonetop-roll-readout">
		{{#if outcome}}<span class="stonetop-roll-outcome">{{outcome.label}}</span>
		{{else if dice.formula}}<span class="stonetop-roll-formula">{{dice.formula}}</span>{{/if}}
		{{!-- `dice-tooltip` is the class core scopes its DICE DISPLAY to, and carrying it is how these
		      dice get core's die faces, its min/max tints and its discarded fade without this system
		      restating any of them. Core's rules for sizing a tooltip are scoped to `.dice-roll` /
		      `.inline-roll`, which a card is neither. --}}
		<div class="stonetop-roll-dice dice-tooltip">
			<ol class="dice-rolls">
				{{#each dice.rolls}}<li class="roll {{classes}}">{{result}}</li>{{/each}}
			</ol>
			{{#if dice.mod}}<span class="stonetop-roll-mod">{{dice.mod}}</span>{{/if}}
			{{#if dice.modeLabel}}<span class="stonetop-roll-mode stonetop-roll-mode--{{dice.rollMode}}">{{dice.modeLabel}}</span>{{/if}}
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
{{/if}}
{{!-- What the roll DID to the sheet that asked for it, in the same words and off the same record the
      sheet's own step prints. Context, not hash params — the record answers through prototype
      getters. --}}
{{#if applied}}{{> stonetop.steading-applied-line applied}}{{/if}}
{{#if resultText.raw}}<div class="stonetop-move-result stonetop-move-result--{{outcome.key}}">{{rich resultText}}</div>{{/if}}
{{#if description.raw}}<div class="stonetop-move-description{{#if dice}} stonetop-move-description--secondary{{/if}}">{{rich description}}</div>{{/if}}
{{#each results}}
<div class="stonetop-move-result stonetop-move-result--{{key}}"><span class="stonetop-move-result-label">{{label}}</span> {{rich text}}</div>
{{/each}}
{{#if xpLine}}{{{xpLine}}}{{/if}}
